### =====================================================================
### Session 4 demos (tag s4-demos). Grouped to match the slides:
### SHOW FIRST, LIVE DEMO 1, LIVE DEMO 2, LIVE DEMO 3, then the cold-reads.
### VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy into Postman.
### Before class: npm install, then run section 1 of requests/s4-demos.sql.
### 0099826704 copy 1 and 0099895102 copy 1 are the only seed copies that
### start available (Status 'D'). Test book 0000000003 has copies 1 and 2.
### =====================================================================


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### SHOW FIRST ("What you'll build" slide): rent 200, again 409, bad copy 400
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Rent it (200)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/1/rent

### Rent it again (409)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/1/rent

### Bad copy number (400, Joi's message)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/0/rent

### Put it back (200) so Live Demo 1 starts clean
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/1/return


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### LIVE DEMO 1: Rent It Twice (end of Check, Then Write)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1) Rent (S4-A3, two helpers): 200, Status 'M'
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/1/rent

### 2) Same request again: 409, checkAvailable() said no, markRented() never ran
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/1/rent

### 3) No copy 9 on the test book: 404
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0000000003/copies/9/rent

### 4a) Reset with the return route (Lab 9): 200
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/1/return

### 4b) The "before" route (S4-B1, everything inline): the same 200
PUT http://localhost:3000/putrentinlinedemo/0099826704/copies/1

### Reset afterwards (200)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/1/return


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### JOI COLD-READ (prediction + answer slides). Test book 0000000003.
### Optional: run after the answer slide if the class wants proof.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### a) 1.00: 400 from Joi, updateRate never runs
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0000000003/copies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rentalRate": 1.00 }

### b) 3.50: 200 and the updated row
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0000000003/copies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rentalRate": 3.50 }

### c) empty body: 400, rentalRate is required
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0000000003/copies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ }


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### LIVE DEMO 2: Shape or Row? (right after Cashier or Kitchen?)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1a) copyNo 0: 400 (bad shape)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/0/rent

### 1b) copyNo abc: 400 (bad shape)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/abc/rent

### 2) ISBN too short: 400 (bad shape)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/123/copies/1/rent

### 3) Good shape, no copy 99: 404 (only the lookup can tell)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704/copies/99/rent

### 4) 1.00: 400 from Joi before any query (Session 3 got a 500 from the CHECK constraint)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/0000000003/copies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rentalRate": 1.00 }


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### LIVE DEMO 3: Search, Then Break It (end of Failing Safely)
### Nothing is deleted in 4: the helper's table name is misspelt on purpose.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1) A search: only matching titles (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/books?title=the

### 2) No title: every book (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/books

### 3) Nothing matches: 200 and [], not 404
GET http://localhost:3000/books?title=zzzz

### 4a) No try (S4-B2): Express's default 500 page (HTML), no JSON
DELETE http://localhost:3000/deletecopynotrydemo/0000000003/copies/2

### 4b) With try (S4-B3): 500 with { "error": "Database error" }, real error in the terminal
DELETE http://localhost:3000/deletecopytrydemo/0000000003/copies/2


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### COLD-READ SNIPPETS A to D: instructor check only.
### Run section 1 of requests/s4-demos.sql first.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Snippet A: 200 ...
PUT http://localhost:3000/s4-snippet-a/books/0099826704/copies/1/rent

### Snippet A again: 200 AGAIN, the copy was already rented. Reset with section 2 of the .sql.
PUT http://localhost:3000/s4-snippet-a/books/0099826704/copies/1/rent

### Snippet B: passes every field check, then 500 (copy 2 already exists: primary key)
POST http://localhost:3000/s4-snippet-b/books/0000000003/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 2, "rentalRate": 3.00 }

### Snippet C: 1.00 hits the CHECK constraint, no try: Express's default 500 page
PUT http://localhost:3000/s4-snippet-c/books/0000000003/copies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rentalRate": 1.00 }

### Snippet D: no title: 200 and [] (compare Live Demo 3 step 2: every book)
GET http://localhost:3000/s4-snippet-d/books
